# .gitignore keeps personal data out of git; this file governs what the
# Vercel CLI actually uploads on `vercel deploy`, which is a separate
# concern — the MCP deployment needs data/selector.duckdb (14MB, the
# warehouse the tools query) even though it must never be committed.
# Everything else large or irrelevant to the deployed function stays out.

.venv/
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
node_modules/

.env
my_spotify_data.zip

data/raw/
data/audio/
data/flywire/
data/essentia_models/
data/lyrics/
data/runs/
data/dj_runs/
data/splits/
data/*.parquet
data/labels.jsonl
data/labels_gold.jsonl
data/.audio_resolve_checkpoint.jsonl

notebooks/
tests/
scripts/
docs/
image.png
uv.lock
PROMPT-PACK.md
Selector — Project Plan.md

# Vercel's Python builder prefers `uv sync` against pyproject.toml over
# `pip install -r requirements.txt` when it finds this file — and
# pyproject.toml's dependency list is the full local dev set (librosa,
# torch, scikit-learn, matplotlib, ...), which blew the 500MB bundle limit
# (859MB) on the first deploy attempt. Excluding it forces the builder onto
# requirements.txt, which lists only what api/index.py actually imports.
pyproject.toml
